    "summary": "Most offices in Galkayo's district administration remained closed for a second day as workers protest unpaid wages. The strike has disrupted public services in the town.",
    "content": "Most municipal offices in Galkayo have been closed for a second consecutive day, as district employees stage a sit-in over unpaid salaries. The workers, who have not received their wages for several months, shut down operations at the local government headquarters and other administrative buildings, halting public services such as document processing and utility payments.\n\nThe strike began early this week when employees at the Galkayo District Administration demanded immediate payment of their arrears. Many workers say they have been forced to take on second jobs to support their families, and that the prolonged non-payment has made it difficult to meet basic needs.\n\nLocal officials have not yet issued a public statement on the matter, but sources within the administration indicate that negotiations are underway. The Galkayo district, which is split between Puntland and Galmudug administrations due to its unique political status, has faced recurring budget shortfalls, exacerbated by rising insecurity and a decline in local revenue collection.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, many of whom have relatives and business interests in Galkayo, this disruption highlights the fragility of local governance in the region. Remittances from diaspora communities often help families cope during such service interruptions, but the prolonged closure of municipal offices could delay transactions and paperwork essential for businesses, land registration, and travel documents.\n\nCommunity leaders have called on both Puntland and Galmudug authorities to address the workers' grievances promptly to prevent a full administrative collapse. The situation remains unresolved as workers vow to continue the strike until their salaries are paid.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/shaqaalaha-dowladda-hoose-ee-galkacyo-oo-mushahar-laaan-ka-cabanaya/424770/",
